  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened capacity for the development of sustainable enterprises</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Dominica has a strong cooperative past and a high cooperative density compared to the size of their populations. However their policy and regulatory framework is strongly outdated. Dominica has requested ILO&apos;s support to assess their cooperative environmenta and to develop a National Cooperative Policy to promote cooperatives in alignment with international standards like the ILO Recommendation 193 and Resolution on Decent Work and the Social and Solidarity Economy. This policy will address the challenges and opportunities faced by cooperative societies, their contribution to the economy, and potential for innovation and expansion. For this ILO will work with all key stakeholders and provide direct technical input to the Cooperative Division under the Ministry of Youth, Culture and Sports.
The new policy will benefit the largely rural Dominica in developing its productive sectors as fisheries and agriculture, lowering costs for individual producers and generating added value.</narrative>
  </description>
